  "notes": "Microsoft Fluent UI styled desktop RSS reader (Fluent Reader). Image cards are distinctive: the article image sits on the top 144px and a blurred, tinted copy of it fills the rest of the card behind the source/title text, giving each card a soft color wash; text-only cards are plain white with title + snippet. Orange dot next to timestamp marks unread; read items lose the dot. Sidebar uses Windows-style grey (#edebe9) with a blue left selection bar and favicon squares per feed. Title bar mimics native window chrome (minimize/maximize/close). Live page defaulted to Magazine view; capture is Card view. Article opens as a modal overlay with prev/next arrows and read/star/full-text/browser actions."
